@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] =
        "Learn what information Comfy Capy Calories stores, why we use it and the choices you have.";
    ViewData["CanonicalUrl"] = "https://calories.comfycapy.com/Privacy";
    ViewData["Robots"] = "index,follow";
}

<div class="content-page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        The short version: Comfy Capy Calories only stores the information it needs to run the app.
        We don't use your data for advertising and we don't add analytics tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
        When you create an account, we store the details you provide, such as your username,
        first name and email address. We also store the security information needed to keep your
        account working, including information used for sign-in, email confirmation, password
        resets and optional two-factor authentication.
    </p>

    <h2>Your profile and calorie goals</h2>
    <p>
        If you complete your profile, we store the information needed to calculate your calorie
        estimates and goals. This can include your date of birth, height, weight, calculation sex,
        activity level, goal, optional goal weight and weekly goal, along with preferences such as
        your measurement system, calorie target and theme.
    </p>

    <h2>Your foods and Diary</h2>
    <p>
        Your custom foods, saved meals, favourites and Diary entries are linked to your account.
        When you log something in your Diary, we keep the nutrition information that applied at
        the time. This means that editing a food later won't unexpectedly change your previous
        Diary entries.
    </p>
    <p>
        Food information from external food databases may be stored by Comfy Capy so it can be
        reused efficiently. These food records aren't treated as your personal data simply because
        they appear in a search. Your favourites, saved meals and Diary activity remain linked to
        your account.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Comfy Capy</h2>
    <p>
        We store the customisation items available to your account and the appearance you've
        chosen for your Capy. This lets your Capy stay the way you left them when you come back.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        Comfy Capy uses cookies that are necessary for features such as signing in, keeping your
        session secure and protecting forms and requests. We don't add advertising or analytics
        tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside services</h2>
    <p>
        Comfy Capy uses external services where they're needed to provide parts of the app. Food
        searches can use external food-data providers, and our email provider handles transactional
        emails such as account messages and feedback delivery.
    </p>

    <h2>Anonymous feedback</h2>
    <p>
        You can send feedback whether you're signed in or signed out. The feedback form doesn't
        ask you to identify yourself, so please don't include personal or sensitive information
        in your message.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
        Your account settings provide options to download your personal account data or permanently
        delete your account. If you have a privacy question that isn't answered here, you can use
        the <a asp-page="/Feedback">Feedback page</a>. Please don't include sensitive information
        in your message.
    </p>
</div>